@Jeff P.

I have...several times. "Oh, those are nice shoes. What are they?" Because they always look so comfortable in their shoes. 

Unlike the newscasters and meteorologists I've noted who teeter on five-inch spike heels.

@Jeff P.

I bought my first pair of HOKAs (and speaking of "pair, I wanted 59D to be PANT) 15 years ago when my work had me standing for long hours.  Now I'm retired and I still wear them every day.  Comfy, supportive, solved my sore ankle problems.

I should earn a commission.

