I always thought of Oklahoma as part of the Midwest. Of the states that border it, I think it resembles Kansas the most...mostly flat, lots of farmland, conservative, kind of laconic. Pretty much everyone else considers it either part of the South, the West, or just a somehow shabbier version of Texas.

