My upper-midwestern great uncle always called it "pop".  Somewhere he'd picked up and had in his garage (where he lived), one of those  Coca Cola machines that sold bottles of Coke back when Coke came in bottles.  You had to put a quarter in to pull out a bottle.  He'd rigged the machine so that the quarter fell back into the return change pocket, so you could use the same quarter every time. 

 My sister and I though he was the coolest guy in the world.

